o the barrier.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":15},{"lap":4,"text":"On the same lap, John Watson bumped Laffite's Ligier from behind, breaking the nose on his Penske. Laffite was spun around by the contact and dropped from eighth to fourteenth place.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":3},{"lap":5,"text":"Meanwhile, Lauda made his way by Depailler on lap five and took second place, seven seconds behind Regazzoni, who was beginning to seem untouchable.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":1},{"lap":20,"text":"At about the same time as Andretti's retirement from the race, Depailler spun and dropped from third to seventh, and after 20 laps, Regazzoni led by 13 seconds over Lauda, Jody Scheckter and Tom Pryce in the Shadow.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":2},{"lap":34,"text":"When Pryce broke a driveshaft on lap 33 and Scheckter had a front wishbone snap on lap 34, Depailler was back in third place, behind the two Ferraris.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":2},{"lap":79,"text":"Then, on the next to last lap, with only first and fifth gears left, he was also overtaken by Fittipaldi, who scored the first Championship point for his own Copersucar team.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":5},{"lap":80,"text":"Regazzoni took an easy win, the fourth of his career, completing the grand chelem of pole position, fastest lap, victory, and leading every lap.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0}],"x":{"drivers":[],"cars":[{"id":"parnelli_1976","ref":"parnelli","name":"Parnelli","year":1976,"pace":-0.08,"pace_sd":0.5,"deg_rel":0.0,"n_races":2,"p_mech_lap":0.00692,"colours":null,"source":"history"}]}}